From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] DPP: accept the Multi-AP backhaul netRoles in Network
 Introduction

A Multi-AP Controller signs a Connector with netRole "mapBackhaulSta"
for a backhaul STA and one with netRole "mapBackhaulBss" for a backhaul
BSS. The Multi-AP specification (v6.1 section 5.3.3, Table 8) makes the
two compatible in the connector group comparison of Easy Connect 3.0
section 6.6.2, and asks for a case insensitive match.
dpp_compatible_netrole() accepts only "sta" with "ap", so the Peer
Discovery between a backhaul STA and a backhaul BSS ends with
STATUS_NO_MATCH and the DPP AKM cannot be used on the backhaul.

Accept the backhaul pair as well. The other pairs of Table 8 (mapAgent
with mapAgent or mapController) apply to the 1905 layer only and never
reach this function.

Report the change as the build feature "dpp-map", so that a Multi-AP
Agent offers the DPP AKM for its backhaul only where this change is in.
The build_features.h hunk is OpenWrt only and is not for upstream.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/common/dpp.c
+++ b/src/common/dpp.c
@@ -4095,10 +4095,20 @@ fail:
 }
 
 
+static int dpp_compatible_map_netrole(const char *role1, const char *role2)
+{
+	return (os_strcasecmp(role1, "mapBackhaulSta") == 0 &&
+		os_strcasecmp(role2, "mapBackhaulBss") == 0) ||
+		(os_strcasecmp(role1, "mapBackhaulBss") == 0 &&
+		 os_strcasecmp(role2, "mapBackhaulSta") == 0);
+}
+
+
 static int dpp_compatible_netrole(const char *role1, const char *role2)
 {
 	return (os_strcmp(role1, "sta") == 0 && os_strcmp(role2, "ap") == 0) ||
-		(os_strcmp(role1, "ap") == 0 && os_strcmp(role2, "sta") == 0);
+		(os_strcmp(role1, "ap") == 0 && os_strcmp(role2, "sta") == 0) ||
+		dpp_compatible_map_netrole(role1, role2);
 }
 
 
--- a/src/utils/build_features.h
+++ b/src/utils/build_features.h
@@ -66,6 +66,8 @@ static inline int has_feature(const char
 #ifdef CONFIG_DPP
 	if (!strcmp(feat, "dpp"))
 		return 1;
+	if (!strcmp(feat, "dpp-map"))
+		return 1;
 #endif
 	return 0;
 }
